meta-diary is a custom Yocto layer created as coursework 
embedded Linux / Yocto Project course. It customizes a minimal Linux
image for QEMU targets: adding a diary-branded image, configuration and
services, a custom character-device kernel module, kernel hardening
fragments, and a set of BSP and BusyBox customizations.

Primary target machine:  qemux86-64  (qemuarm64 also used)
Yocto release:           scarthgap
License:                 MIT (see COPYING.MIT)


Dependencies
============

  URI:    git://git.yoctoproject.org/poky
  layers: meta, meta-poky
  branch: scarthgap


Table of Contents
=================

  I.   Adding the meta-diary layer to your build
  II.  Layer contents
  III. Building the diary image
  IV.  Misc


I. Adding the meta-diary layer to your build
============================================

Clone the layer next to your poky checkout, source the build
environment, then add the layer:

  bitbake-layers add-layer /path/to/meta-diary

This registers meta-diary in conf/bblayers.conf.


II. Layer contents
==================

conf/
    Layer configuration (layer.conf): collection name, priority,
    and scarthgap compatibility.

recipes-core/
    images/diary-image.bb
                     The main image recipe. A minimal systemd-based
                     image with the diary customizations installed.
    base-files       bbappend that resolves a motd file conflict.
    busybox          bbappend adding a build marker to the BusyBox
                     banner via a devtool-generated patch.

recipes-diary/
    diary-config     Branding and services: motd, a diary-version
                     file, and a heartbeat systemd service.
    diary-httpd      A small HTTP service packaged as a systemd unit.
    diary-char       A custom character-device kernel module, built
                     as an out-of-tree module and autoloaded at boot.
                     Exposes a 'verbose' module parameter.

recipes-kernel/
    linux-yocto bbappend with kernel configuration fragments for
    the diary device, security hardening, 9p and Hyper-V support.

recipes-bsp/
    u-boot           bbappend with bootloader customizations.

recipes-fun/
    sl               The classic 'sl' steam-locomotive joke program,
                     built from its git source, as a packaging exercise.

recipes-example/
    example          A minimal example recipe used for learning the
                     recipe format.


III. Building the diary image
=============================

With the build environment sourced and meta-diary added to your
build, run:

  bitbake diary-image

The resulting image can be booted under QEMU with:

  runqemu qemux86-64


IV. Misc
========

This layer is coursework and is not intended for production use.
Host-specific build configuration (local.conf) is not included in
this repository; only the layer itself is versioned here.
